Modifications to upstream files
------------------------------

Provided in accordance with Apache License 2.0, Section 4(b). The following
files from the upstream snapshot have been changed in this repository:

  * LICENSE
        Added. The upstream snapshot omitted it because xr-ai ships a LICENSE
        at its own repository root; this repository is standalone, and every
        source file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 header.
        Copied verbatim from xr-ai.

  * .gitignore
        Anchored root-only directory patterns with a leading "/". The
        unanchored forms matched at any depth and hid 14 already-tracked
        files. Removed the "tests/" rule (the repository tracks test sources)
        and the ".github/" rule (it blocked CI workflow files). Generalised
        "semantic_slam_server.egg-info/" to "*.egg-info/".

  * pyproject.toml
        Added an "asr" optional-dependency group declaring openai-whisper and
        faster-whisper, which slam/services/asr.py imports but which were
        previously undeclared.

  * README.md
        Corrected a dangling link to THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md (this repository
        ships THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) and updated the licensing paragraph to
        reference LICENSE and pyproject.toml.

  * THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
        Removed the torchaudio entry and the sentence describing setup.py's
        dependency set, following the removal of setup.py. torchaudio is not
        imported anywhere in this source tree.

  * setup.py
        Removed. pyproject.toml declares a [build-system] using hatchling, so
        PEP 517 builds already ignored setup.py. It had drifted to a different
        package name and referenced an entry point module not present in the
        tree.


Additions
---------

Branches other than "main" contain work that is not part of the upstream
snapshot, including Quest streaming support, merge/GOBS performance
diagnostics, human-ignore filtering, and ILLIXR integration via the
semantic_python relay.

